---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AppStoreCta from "../../components/AppStoreCta.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Passport in Photos — Passport Pack guide"
  description="Why a passport copy in Apple Photos is a bad vault — and how Passport Pack keeps scans encrypted off the camera roll."
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <div class="container prose-page__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Guide</p>
      <h1 class="display prose-page__title">Your passport isn’t a photo.</h1>
      <p class="prose-page__lede muted">
        Snapping a passport page into Apple Photos feels convenient until Recents, iCloud Photos, and
        every library-access app can see it.
      </p>

      <section class="prose-block">
        <h2>What goes wrong in Photos</h2>
        <p>
          Photos is built for everyday pictures: sync, search, shared albums, and third-party apps
          that request full library access. A passport scan sitting next to screenshots inherits that
          model. It is easy to forward, easy to leave unlocked on a shared device, and easy to forget
          when you wipe Recents.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>iCloud Photos can replicate the image across devices you did not intend.</li>
          <li>Apps with Photos permission can read identity documents without a vault unlock.</li>
          <li>There is no master-password gate on a JPEG in the camera roll.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="prose-block">
        <h2>What a vault should do instead</h2>
        <p>
          Passport Pack scans the document into an AES-GCM encrypted store under your master password.
          The image is not written to Photos. Face ID can unlock the vault for convenience, but it is
          not the content key — lose the master password and Passport Pack cannot recover the archive.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="prose-block">
        <h2>Practical next step</h2>
        <p>
          If you already have a passport copy in Photos, scan a fresh copy into Passport Pack, confirm
          the fields, then delete the Photos original (and Recently Deleted). Free Passport Pack covers
          three documents on Me so you can prove the workflow before upgrading.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="prose-cta">
        <AppStoreCta />
        <a class="prose-link" href={withBase("/security")}>How encryption works →</a>
        <a class="prose-link" href={withBase("/guides/family-travel-documents")}>Family travel docs guide →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
